    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0529" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v01/pg497"/>

                <head>236. Telegram From the Secretary of State to the Embassy in Vietnam<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d236-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-07-26T18:01:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26,
                                1955—6:01 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>293. …</p>
                <p>When Molotov brought up Vietnamese elections [at the Eden–Molotov talks held in
                    Geneva on July 23] Eden stated British had always suggested consultations and
                    U.S. UK France had agreed recommend Vietnamese Government answer Dong letter.
                    Molotov had seen report of agreement in press.</p>
                <p>Macmillan declared UK would do best see Geneva Accords fully implemented and
                    consultations undertaken.</p>
                <p>Eden doubted two co-Chairmen should send communication other Geneva signatories.
                    Molotov did not dissent. British thought preferable co-Chairmen maintain close
                    contact two parties Viet-Nam, Indians and each other. Molotov appeared accept
                    idea of telegram to Nehru in this sense.</p>
                <p>Molotov stated he would send Nehru own account conversation and asked whether
                    Eden would object Molotov’s informing “Chinese” Government. Eden said no.</p>
                <pb facs="0530" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>
                <p>Eden commented atmosphere calm and not unfriendly. Both sides agreed world not so
                    close to war as last summer.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
